      neutralCase: "Bitcoin consolidates around the $66,000-$68,000 range, unable to break decisively higher or lower, as \'summer slumber\' continues with low trading volumes. Ether maintains its gains above $1,900 but struggles to reach $2,100 amidst mixed market signals. Regulatory actions remain localized, having limited immediate impact on global sentiment but contributing to a gradual, long-term shift towards more regulated markets.",
      probabilityWeightedOutlook: "A moderately bullish short-to-medium term outlook with significant caveats. There\'s a 45% chance of Bitcoin breaking $68,000 in the next few weeks due to underlying accumulation, but a 35% chance of rejection and consolidation. Ether has a 60% chance of touching $2,100 given its strong fundamentals. Regulatory developments will likely have a medium-term impact, with a 70% probability of continued global enforcement leading to a more structured but potentially slower growth environment.",
